+# Phorepoc fix: 64-bit host pointer truncation.
+# The stock plugin calls the nvmemmory C library through ctypes with NO
+# argtypes/restype, so every argument defaults to a 32-bit c_int. On our
+# 64-bit qemu-system-arm build both the SyborgNVMemory* object pointer
+# (nvmem_create's return) and the shared-memory HOST pointer (memregion
+# host addr, e.g. 0x7f3d90a5c000) are 64-bit -- truncation made nvmem_read
+# scribble through a bogus 32-bit pointer and SIGSEGV qemu the moment the
+# FAT mount issued its first media transaction. Declare the real signatures
+# (nvmemmory.h): create->void*, obj args void*, host addr void*, the rest
+# int32/uint32.
 #
